<title>USA: Wisconsin jobless rate at 3.5 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Wisconsin jobless rate at 3.5 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wisconsin's unemployment was 3.5 percent last year, the lowest rate for the state since 1969 when the jobless rate stood at 3.3 percent, the state's department of workforce development reported this week.</p>
<p>The department also reported the seasonally adjusted December jobless rate rose to 3.5 percent from 3.1 percent in November.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
</text>
